# BUGS

The theme chosen isn't kept: each start puts Platinum Indigo in force, and themes don't yet follow workspaces or apps.
The frame's edges are made from a small one's, so a body whose gradient or pattern changes along an edge has its middle repeated there.
Every face in `/lib/fonts` is read whole when Radharc starts, those the theme doesn't name too.
High contrast is a variant to choose, not yet one switch over every theme.
While Radharc reads `/dev/kbd`, the console's shell hears no keys, and nothing else shows its text.
Keys don't repeat, and the keyboard's layout is kbdfs's starting keymap, not a changed one.
Only an image's alpha, and a frame's, are blended: a solid layer is opaque, a window has no opacity of its own, and the cursor is drawn in a one-bit shape, so nothing at its edges is blended.
Other transfers and primaries are refused, not converted: the display's colour isn't known, and is taken to be sRGB.
There is no direct scanout, no display driver and no GPU; the screen is the boot framebuffer's size.
Of the gated services only `shortcuts` is there, and there are no secure surfaces: a manifest's `grant windows` lines other than `prompt`, `chooser`, `layout`, `shortcuts`, `clipboard` and `lock` are refused.
For a question asked on `prompt`, `session` and `always` are words for its asker to keep: Radharc records only its own gated services' grants.
A tiled workspace's area is the whole screen, so a panel, such as Deskbar's, covers the tiled windows beneath it.
There is one output, and the workspaces' count is read only when Radharc starts.
An app's frame is kept by its name alone, so two windows of one app share one, the last closed.
Switching workspaces and modes isn't animated.
Its text is in the console's 8 by 16 font.
A key or button held down when the prompt shows never comes up for the window that had it.
The clipboard is at `/svc/windows`, not yet in each window's `/dev` but a rio window's.
Nothing empties the clipboard but a secret entry's end.
A client killed between two representations of an entry commits the ones it finished.
While the chooser confirms one window's file, another window's `choose` is refused as `unavailable`.
The clock is UTC: there are no time zones yet.
A clock's minute is a frame of Radharc's even on an idle desktop; `status` counts those frames apart.
